  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRC Refugees Voluntary Repatriation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to provide dignified, safe and orderly voluntary return of 700 Congolese refugees back to their places of origin in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) from Lovua settlement in Lunda Norte Province - Angola. IOM provides transport assistance to the respective refugees to the designated way stations before the border and to the identified transit centres at border points between DRC and Angola, where they are further be assisted to reach their specific areas of origin in DRC by UNHCR. IOM registers refugees&#x2019; luggage, follow up on passenger manifests, assists vulnerable refugees to board the trucks and load/offload their belongings. During the convoy, IOM provides escorts for refugees to ensure their needs are met during travel.</narrative>
  </description>
